{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));art=r['artifacts'][-1];state=json.load(open('../state.json'));issue=next(x for x in state['review_issues'] if x['id']=='f56328eaf209418a8550bf79986a86ce')\nlimits=['Leader state and expired marker are constructed local premises, not an observed elected-cluster history.','Manual checkLeaderLease does not establish automatic timer scheduling or total role-retention duration.','Heartbeat, ordinary fallback after pipeline return, incoming RPC, snapshot and verification workers are omitted; they may change a full-node endpoint.','No client success, stale application read, wrong commitment or crash/recovery consequence is observed.','Two operations are independent scenarios, not one combined execution history.','Higher-term heartbeat rejection variant remains unresolved and outside the no-reply obligation.']\nsources=['src-lease-contract','src-lease','src-pipeline-contract','src-inmem-pipeline-timeout','src-inmem-pipeline-send','src-pipeline-reply','src-append-reply','src-default-and-valid-config']\nrationale='Reviewed fixed artifact version 2 and raw execution 55c79fd4cf55497a81166bce840a1c45, not draft intentions. Compared captured plans: all metadata, prerequisites and oracle are identical; executable diff only sets HeartbeatTimeout and ElectionTimeout to 2s and requires ValidateConfig success before prefix emission. Both scenarios passed that call and completed, resolving the old invalid-input challenge for the corrected artifact only. Applicability: the public no-quorum-contact lease promise applies conditionally to two Voters with expired prior remote contact and no receiver processing or reply; timeout is not being equated with no processing in general. Here no receiver Raft runs and no Respond call occurs. Decomposition: actual InmemTransport timeout producer, same returned future/request, actual pipelineDecode and checkLeaderLease span the selected fact lifecycle. Future timeout alone is not the oracle; actual role after lease decision is. Ordinary timeout supplies a permitted comparison, not the normative source. Even satisfying this obligation would not suffice for consensus correctness; alternate writers and workers remain outside scope. Correspondence: lease_result is the independent result trigger; assertion state == Follower follows the no-contact contract for this constructed prefix. operation identifies each separate scenario, not the compared state or contact value. completed.contact_before_ns references prefix.contact_ns to require causal order. No result is a prerequisite. Fixed harness establishes four-second prior age and structurally excludes new contact; output verifies pipeline command timed out and same_request=true. Decoder completion precedes manual lease check. Raw output has eight parsed events, no parse loss, pipeline result 3 associated with prefix 0/completion 2 and ordinary result 7 with prefix 4/completion 6. Pipeline contact changes from 1790487790947517534 to 1790487794990072973 with age 30901ns then State is Leader; ordinary contact stays 1790487790991020920 with age 4041948335ns then State is Follower. Thus antecedent and completed comparison are nonvacuous in these executed local scenarios. Awaiting Error before decoder is an observation adaptation that does not set response/contact or produce a synthetic reply. No protocol code was changed; controls stop on completion, and tool timeout would be an incomplete result. No further correspondence issue found within this conditional scope; this is a provisional scoped review, not overall correctness or independent replication.'\ns={'action':'review','artifact_id':art['id'],'rationale':'Review corrected artifact and fresh execution, resolving the specific configuration issue while preserving independent history/consequence boundaries. The old artifact remains invalid for supported-input attribution; the new measurement is reviewed on its own bytes and events.','review_items':[{'target_id':art['id'],'aspect':'checker_correspondence','status':'no_issue_found','source_ids':sources,'rationale':rationale,'counterevidence':[],'limitations':limits}],'resolutions':[{'issue_id':issue['id'],'target_version':art['version'],'original_question':issue['explanation'],'source_ids':sources,'rationale':'The exact issue was lease 2s with default heartbeat/election 1s and no validation. Captured version 2 changes heartbeat/election to 2s and executes ValidateConfig before either local_prefix; raw completed execution reaches both results with no validation failure. Source config.go permits equality, so this removes that specific configuration invalidity. Plan metadata and state oracle are unchanged, and the discrepancy is remeasured in the new execution. This does not retroactively approve version 1 or establish a legal election prefix.','residual_issue_ids':[],'scope_limitations':limits}], 'feedback':{'ref_ids':[art['id'],'55c79fd4cf55497a81166bce840a1c45',issue['id']],'answered':'The corrected supported configuration executes and preserves the complete conditional local witness. Pipeline timeout refreshes contact and produces Leader after lease consumption; ordinary timeout produces Follower. Focused review resolves configuration invalidity for version 2, not the old artifact.','remaining':limits,'understanding':'unchanged','rationale':'The most limiting remaining relation is a legal elected-cluster prefix with real pipeline activation and active protective workers. Any continuation should test that same timeout lifecycle and actual scheduled/public endpoint rather than infer it from this local comparison.'}}\njsonschema.validate(s,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-review-corrected.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('Corrected artifact review and explicit resolution validate')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit